An analysis of $B^{+} 	o D^{+} \overline{
u}_{\ell} \ell^{-}$ decays where $\ell$ is either an electron or muon, was carried out in the Belle detector using a dataset of 772 million $B\overline{B}$ events recorded at the $\Upsilon(4S)$ $\Upsilon(4S)$ resonance with the Belle detector at the KEKB collider. The results of a search for $B^{+} 	o D_{s}^{+} \overline{
u}_{\ell} \ell^{-}$ decays yielded no significant results and an upper bound for the branching fraction of $B^{+} 	o D_{s}^{+} \overline{
u}_{\ell} \ell^{-}$ was found to be 7.9 times $10^{-4}$ at a 95% confidence level over a range of $\mathcal{B}(B^{+} 	o D_{s}^{+} \overline{
u}_{\ell} \ell^{-})$ as a function of $\mathcal{B}(B^{+} 	o D^{+} \overline{
u}_{\ell} \ell^{-})$.
